{"id": "1.2-00040", "case_id": "opencores_memory_acs32_v1", "parent_id": null, "source": "opencores/system_controller_memory_controller_ip_core", "record_protocol": null, "panels": {"stored": "<h2>Agent task and scoring</h2><div class='card'><table><tbody><tr><th style='width:175px'>Input task</th><td class='path'>Project specification, interfaces, and permitted public assets</td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Agent context</th><td class='path'>Direct agent workspace: <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00040&amp;file_q=public%2F'>public/</a> (6 files)</td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Expected output</th><td class='path'>Required RTL: rtl/verilog/mc_adr_sel.v, rtl/verilog/mc_cs_rf.v, rtl/verilog/mc_dp.v, rtl/verilog/mc_incn_r.v, rtl/verilog/mc_mem_if.v, rtl/verilog/mc_obct.v, rtl/verilog/mc_obct_top.v, rtl/verilog/mc_rd_fifo.v and 5 more. <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00040&amp;file=public%2Foutput_contract.json'>Open full output contract</a></td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Hidden reference</th><td class='path'>13 RTL files under private/reference/; <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00040&amp;file=private%2Freference%2Frtl%2Fverilog%2Fmc_adr_sel.v'>open first reference file</a></td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Private score</th><td class='path'>Passed verification testpoints divided by total testpoints, using testbenches or formal verification<br><strong>5 verification testpoints:</strong> registers, external_reads, two_regions, byte_masks, write_protect. <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00040&amp;file=private%2Fscoring.json'>Open private scoring contract</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>Case-stored agent instruction</h2><div class='card'><p class='muted'>These are case-stored instructions. A launcher may add framing or execution limits; its saved trajectory is the exact runtime record.</p><details><summary>public/instruction.md · <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00040&amp;file=public%2Finstruction.md'>Open raw</a></summary><pre># Implement the memory controller project\nImplement the complete required source closure and mc_top integration from the\noriginal Memory Controller IP Core specification. This case fixes the default\npreprocessed configuration (CS0/CS1 implemented; remaining regions disabled),\nwith two 32-bit asynchronous chip-select memory devices. Other SDRAM/SSRAM/SCS\noperating modes and narrower devices are outside this configuration&#x27;s scoring.\nInternal modules and the dummy CS module remain required at their declared paths.\n\nWishbone is32 bits, byte addressed. clk_i period10ns and mc_clk_i20ns; rst_i is\nactive high. Hold cyc/stb,address,we,sel,data until ack or err. The register region\nis address[31:29]=3 and memory region is address[31:29]=0. Registers start at\n0x60000000: CSR+0, read-only POC+4, BA_MASK+8, CSC0+0x10,TMS0+0x14,\nCSC1+0x18,TMS1+0x1c. Use full-word register writes. POC captures mc_data_pad_i\naround reset; the evaluator supplies zero during that interval and gives320\nmemory clocks to settle the default power-on delay before configuration.\n\nFor the scored configuration set BA_MASK=0xff, CSC0=0x00000025 and\nCSC1=0x00800025 (EN=1,type=2 ACS,BW=2 for32bits,parity disabled).\nThus chip0 covers byte addresses starting0, chip1 starts0x10000000; each selection\ncompares CSC[23:16] against address[28:21], masked by BA_MASK[7:0].\nTMS0/TMS1=0x00222204: read-data-valid counter4, read-to-high-Z2,\nwrite-pulse-width2, write-disable2, write-high2. Retain timing-register read/write\nbehavior. The original TMS timing units and pipeline overhead apply.\n\nPhysical ACS address is byte-address bits25:2 for32-bit devices. CS/WE/OE are\nactive low. mc_doe_pad_doe_o is active-high output drive. The peripheral supplies\nread data while CS and OE are asserted. Selected writes preserve bytes masked by\nDQM; DQM is the inverse of Wishbone sel for writes (bit0 is bits7:0). Tests also\nread device data initialized privately before any bus write, so implement actual\nexternal memory reads and writes. Pins mc_br=0,mc_ack=1,mc_sts=0,parity inputs0;\nsuspend/resume held0. Distinct regions must not be selected together.\n\nCSCn[8] write-protect produces a Wishbone error and leaves device data unchanged;\nreads remain allowed. Private points cover register programming, external reads,\nboth regions, byte masks and write protection. Public checks compile only.\nHeaders are resolved; #1 simulation-only assignments and explicitly marked\nsimulation diagnostics are removed privately.\n\nImplement every required path in output_contract.json. Declaration-only ports\nare in interfaces/modules.v. No initial/final, delays, simulation system tasks,\nforce/release or external includes are permitted. Only declared RTL is collected.\nMissing files, forbidden constructs or failed top compilation score zero. Each\nprivate point has equal weight and requires all of its checks to pass. Use\nterminal/file_editor, iverilog, vvp and Python iteratively; finish by saving RTL.\nRun `python3 checks/check.py` for public compilation feedback.\n</pre></details></div>"}, "files": [{"name": "case.json", "url": "assets/640872025a765b1d0303bce4b18eada46b959795724d59e995c6698bee04e5eb.txt", "size": 49131, "binary": false, "section": "Other: case.json"}, {"name": "environment/runtime.json", "url": "assets/771e58998dfa59d19bd4591ce49673fcbadd56239829b74d2a9c5869aef77295.txt", "size": 4693, "binary": false, "section": "Other: environment"}, {"name": "private/original_reference/rtl/verilog/mc_adr_sel.v", "url": "assets/31c7f730e43192c26df64ca7bb2f5e22f9084b649fe0627ad5c85af55789fcce.txt", "size": 10803, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/original_reference/rtl/verilog/mc_cs_rf.v", "url": "assets/5da97b3ab64fa7d11a858bef5402d7835abb7bf15f1dec2d77cb072a08a35b23.txt", "size": 8212, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/original_reference/rtl/verilog/mc_defines.v", "url": "assets/d54f237f1baba818fcff23d297e4c1c8c2c